<title>Painful Scrotum: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0370-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>History of recent trauma?</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-2">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Cremasteric reflex present?</label>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Manual detorsionresulting in immediate relief of pain?</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Urologic consultation to consider future orchiopexy.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Doppler ultrasound or scintigraphy readily available (i.e., would not delay surgery beyond 6 hrs from onset)?</label>
<path target="cell-9">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-8">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Emergent urologic consultation for suspected torsion.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-9">
<label>Increased flow (Doppler) or increased uptake (scintigraphy)?</label>
<path target="cell-10">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-8">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>Pursue further testing or treatment of condition (orchitis&#x002F;epididymitis, etc.).</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Asymmetric testes, or a horizontal lie?</label>
<path target="cell-4">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-11">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-11">
<label>Other findings suggestive of a diagnosis other than torsion?</label>
<path target="cell-10">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Pain significantly improved or resolved after one hour?</label>
<path target="cell-12">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-2">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>Likely simple trauma; ice, anti-inflammatories.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
